{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"goal","type":"text","text":"<span class=\"wan-scene-style wan-scene-math wan-scene-grid wan-version-matrix\"></span>\n# Research goal\n\n## Context\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prompt}&\\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{cfg}}\\mathrm{video},&&\\text{consider video generation from a prompt in live mode,}\\\\[6pt]\n\\mathrm{cfg}&\\in\\mathcal C,&&\\text{with configurations from the set C,}\\\\[6pt]\n\\mathrm{FPS}(\\mathrm{cfg})&=\\frac{N_{\\rm frames}}{T_{\\rm generation}(\\mathrm{cfg})}\\ge 15,&&\\text{Live mode requires a rate of at least 15 frames per second.}\\\\[6pt]\nM_{\\rm VRAM}(\\mathrm{cfg})&\\le 8\\ \\text{GB},\\quad M_{\\rm RAM}(\\mathrm{cfg})\\le 16\\ \\text{GB},&&\\text{The difficulty is that memory on the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop graphics card is limited,}\\\\[6pt]\n\\mathcal L(\\mathrm{cfg})&=\\mathrm{LPIPS}_{\\rm align}(\\mathrm{cfg})+\\bigl(1-\\mathrm{DINO}(\\mathrm{cfg})\\bigr).&&\\text{and when video generation is accelerated, the video quality drops, which we measure by the loss.}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n## Goal\n\nFind the configuration that achieves the smallest loss of video quality<br>at a rate of at least 15 frames per second<br>on the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop (8 GB of video memory, 16 GB of RAM).\n\nLet us state the optimization problem\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\min_{\\mathrm{cfg}\\in\\mathcal C}\\quad&\\mathcal L(\\mathrm{cfg})\\\\[8pt]\n\\text{subject to}\\quad&\\mathrm{FPS}(\\mathrm{cfg})\\ge 15,\\\\\n&M_{\\rm VRAM}(\\mathrm{cfg})\\le 8\\ \\text{GB},\\\\\n&M_{\\rm RAM}(\\mathrm{cfg})\\le 16\\ \\text{GB}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n# Task 1\n\nBuild a mathematical model that predicts $\\mathrm{FPS}$, memory and $\\mathcal L$ from a configuration $\\mathrm{cfg}$, so as to discard configurations that violate the constraints even before the experiments.\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{cfg}=\\Bigl(\\underbrace{\\mathrm{cfg}_{\\rm offloading}}_{\\text{system loading plan}},\\quad \\underbrace{\\mathrm{cfg}_{\\rm input}}_{\\text{input}},\\quad \\underbrace{\\mathrm{cfg}_{\\rm text\\ encoder},\\ \\underbrace{\\mathrm{cfg}_{\\rm DiT}}_{\\text{transformer block configuration}},\\ \\mathrm{cfg}_{\\rm VAE}}_{\\text{video generation}}\\Bigr)\n$$\n\n\n\n| Version       | Model                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | Quantization                                                                                                                          | Compilation                                                                                                                                                                  | Resolution change                                                                                   | Offloading                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | Video continuation                                                                                                                  | Scene change                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| :----------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| General model | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned} \\mathrm{prompt}_j&\\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{T5}}\\mathrm{ctx}_j,\\qquad \\mathrm{KVtext}_j=\\mathrm{KV}^{\\rm cross}(\\mathrm{ctx}_j),\\\\[6pt] (\\epsilon_{n+1},\\mathrm{ctx},\\mathrm{KVvid}_n)&\\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{DiT}}(\\mathrm{lat}_{n+1},\\mathrm{KVvid}_{n+1}),\\\\[6pt] \\mathrm{lat}_{n+1}&\\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{VAE}}\\mathrm{frame}_{n+1}. \\end{aligned}$ | $\\displaystyle \\mathcal Q:(W_{\\rm DiT},W_{\\rm T5},\\mathrm{KV})\\mapsto(\\hat W_{\\rm DiT},\\hat W_{\\rm T5},\\widehat{\\mathrm{KV}})$ | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&G=(V,E)\\\\&\\mathcal O:\\ G\\mapsto G'\\\\&\\mathcal C_{\\rm compile}:\\ G'\\xrightarrow{\\rm torch.export}G_{\\rm FX}\\\\&G_{\\rm FX}\\xrightarrow{\\rm AOTInductor}\\mathrm{package}\\end{aligned}$ | $\\displaystyle \\Phi_{\\rm pos}:(\\mathrm{pos},\\theta)\\mapsto(\\mathrm{pos}^{\\prime},\\theta^{\\prime})$ | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\underbrace{G=(V,E)}_{\\text{computational graph}},\\quad\\underbrace{\\mathcal R_i\\subseteq\\mathcal R}_{\\text{resources}}\\\\[5pt]&\\mathrm{plan}^{\\star}\\in\\operatorname*{arg\\,min}_{\\mathrm{plan}}\\widehat t_{\\rm end}(\\mathrm{plan})\\\\[5pt]&M_{\\rm VRAM}\\le B_{\\rm VRAM},\\quad M_{\\rm RAM}\\le B_{\\rm RAM}\\end{aligned}$ | $\\displaystyle \\Phi_{\\rm continue}:(\\epsilon_{n+1},\\mathrm{ctx},\\mathrm{KVvid}_n)\\mapsto(\\mathrm{lat}_{n+1},\\mathrm{KVvid}_{n+1})$ | $\\displaystyle \\Phi_{\\rm scene}:(\\mathrm{KVvid}_0,\\mathrm{KVtext}_0,\\mathrm{prompt}_1)\\mapsto\\begin{cases} (\\varnothing,\\mathrm{KVtext}_1),&\\text{new scene},\\\\[3pt] \\Phi(\\mathrm{KVvid}_0,\\mathrm{KVtext}_0),&\\text{continuation}. \\end{cases}$ |\n\n## MVP1\n\n| Version | Model | Quantization | Compilation | Resolution change | Offloading | Video continuation | Scene change |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| [MVP1](MVP1%20EN.canvas)<br>[MVP1](configs/mvp1.json) | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\mathrm{T5}=\\mathrm{UMT5\\mbox{-}XXL}\\\\&\\mathrm{DiT}:\\ \\mathrm{Wan}\\mapsto\\mathrm{LongLive\\,2.0\\mbox{-}5B\\ S2}\\\\&\\mathrm{decoder}:\\ \\mathrm{Wan\\ VAE}\\mapsto\\mathrm{TAEHV}\\end{aligned}$<br>[Experiments](notes/research/Модель.md) | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\mathcal Q^{(1)}:\\\\[4pt]&W_{\\rm DiT}^{\\rm BF16}\\mapsto\\widehat W_{\\rm DiT}^{\\rm W4A4}&&\\substack{\\mathrm{FPS}:6.28\\to11.29\\\\\\mathrm{FP8}\\to\\mathrm{W4A4},\\ 512\\times928}\\\\&W_{\\rm T5}^{\\rm BF16}\\mapsto\\widehat W_{\\rm T5}^{\\rm INT8}&&T_{\\rm prompt}:2.86\\to1.63\\ \\mathrm{s}\\\\&\\mathrm{KV}^{\\rm BF16}\\mapsto\\widehat{\\mathrm{KV}}^{\\rm FP8\\ E4M3}&&\\substack{M_{\\rm KV}:9.819\\to4.985\\ \\mathrm{GiB}\\\\704\\times1280}\\end{aligned}$<br>[FPS and T5](notes/research/cards/E30.%20%D0%A1%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B0%D1%8F%20%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%87%D0%BA%D0%B0%20W4A4%20704%C3%971280%20%D0%B8%20%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B6%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B5%20%D1%88%D0%B0%D0%B3%D0%B8.md) · [KV size](docs/bf16-native.md) · [In detail](docs/research/mvp1/Quantization.md) | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\mathcal O^{(1)}:\\\\[4pt]&\\mathrm{Attn}_{\\rm self}:\\ \\mathrm{SDPA}\\mapsto\\mathrm{Sage\\,2}&&\\substack{T_{\\rm block}:186.8\\to77.3\\ \\mathrm{ms}\\\\\\mathrm{FP8},\\ 704\\times1280}\\\\&\\mathrm{Attn}_{\\rm cross}:\\ \\mathrm{SDPA}\\mapsto\\mathrm{Sage\\,2}\\\\&\\underbrace{(W_Q,W_K,W_V)\\mapsto W_{\\rm QKV}}_{\\text{self-attention}}\\\\&\\mathrm{FFN}\\mapsto\\underbrace{\\mathrm{GEMM}_1\\to\\mathrm{GELU}\\to\\mathrm{Quant}_4}_{\\text{fuse}}\\to\\mathrm{GEMM}_2\\\\&\\mathrm{RoPE}\\overset{\\rm fuse}{\\hookrightarrow}\\mathrm{Attn}_{\\rm Sage}\\end{aligned}$<br>[In detail](MVP1%20EN.canvas) · [Measurement](notes/research/cards/E29.%20%D0%92%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%88%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0%20A%E2%80%B2%20%D0%B8%20%D1%81%D0%BF%D1%83%D1%81%D0%BA%20B,%20FP8,%20704%C3%971280.md) | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&704\\times1280\\mapsto512\\times928\\\\&\\mathrm{PI},\\quad t=1\\\\&N_{\\rm steps}=2,\\quad\\mathrm{shift}=5\\end{aligned}$<br>[[Позиции RoPE\\|RoPE positions]] | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\mathrm{policy}_1=\\mathrm{greedy\\_ram}\\\\&B_{\\rm VRAM}^{\\rm margin}=1.5\\ \\mathrm{GiB}\\\\&B_{\\rm RAM}^{\\rm margin}=0\\ \\mathrm{GiB}\\\\&B_{\\rm T5}^{\\rm first}=1.0\\ \\mathrm{GiB}\\end{aligned}$<br>[[Offloading]] | $\\displaystyle \\Phi_{\\rm continue}^{(1)}:=\\left.\\Phi_{\\rm continue}\\right\\rvert_{\\substack{F_{\\rm chunk}=8,\\ F_{\\rm anch}=8\\\\F_{\\rm win}=32}}$<br>[[Длительная генерация\\|Long generation]] | $\\displaystyle \\Phi_{\\rm scene}^{(1)}:=\\left.\\Phi_{\\rm scene}\\right\\rvert_{F_{\\rm scene\\ offset}=8}$<br>Mode: not set.<br>[[Смена сцены\\|Scene change]] |\n\n# Task 2\n\nIn MVP1 we assembled a working video generation and chose the ways to speed up and to save memory.\n\nConsider the quality search for MVP2: we start from the 704×1280 reference, choose a starting configuration that fits in memory, and change one factor at a time, comparing the quality loss.\n\nRun experiments measuring $\\mathrm{FPS}$, memory and $\\mathcal L$ for MVP1 and MVP2, to find the configuration with the smallest $\\mathcal L$ at $\\mathrm{FPS}\\ge 15$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\underbrace{\\mathrm{cfg}_0}_{\\text{reference for comparison}}&:\\quad 704\\times1280,\\\\[6pt]\n\\underbrace{\\mathcal C_{\\rm mem}}_{\\text{feasible placement}}&=\\{\\mathrm{cfg}:M_{\\rm VRAM}\\le8\\ \\text{GB},\\ M_{\\rm RAM}\\le16\\ \\text{GB}\\},\\\\[6pt]\n\\underbrace{\\mathrm{cfg}_{\\rm start}}_{\\text{chosen starting point}}&=\\mathrm{point\\mbox{-}b2}\\in\\mathcal C_{\\rm mem},\\\\[6pt]\n\\underbrace{\\mathcal B_{\\rm PI},\\mathcal B_{\\rm NTK}}_{\\text{two search regions}}&\\subseteq\\mathcal C_{\\rm mem},\\\\[6pt]\n\\min_{\\mathrm{cfg}\\in\\mathcal B_b}\\ \\mathcal L(\\mathrm{cfg})\n&\\quad\\text{subject to }\\mathrm{FPS}(\\mathrm{cfg})\\ge15,\\quad b\\in\\{\\mathrm{PI},\\mathrm{NTK}\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPI and NTK define two search regions; the minimum remains the goal of the experiments.\n\nResult 12.11: in both regions the loss changes little, we chose PI by the token grid ratio. We fixed the point by the grids.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{cfg}_{\\rm MVP2}&:\\quad 544\\times960,\\quad\\underbrace{M_H=\\tfrac{22}{17},\\quad M_W=\\tfrac{40}{30}}_{\\text{PI by the grid ratio}},\\quad F_{\\rm win}=32,\\\\[6pt]\n\\overline{\\mathcal L}_1&=0.426,\\qquad\\underbrace{\\mathrm{FPS}=13.44<15}_{\\text{constraint not met}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe nearest point with $\\mathrm{FPS}\\ge15$: $512\\times928$, $\\overline{\\mathcal L}_1=0.484$. The missing $11.6\\%$ of speed we look for in the kernels.\n\n[Start and decisions E30](notes/research/cards/E30.%20Стартовая%20точка%20W4A4%20704×1280%20и%20отложенные%20шаги.md) · [Descent 09.11](D:/Experiments/DIT/outputs/res-descent-2026-11-09/REPORT.md) · [Latest PI / NTK comparisons](docs/STATE.md)\n\n## MVP2\n\n| Version | Model | Quantization | Compilation | Resolution change | Offloading | Video continuation | Scene change |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| [MVP2](MVP2%20EN.canvas) · point fixed 12.11<br>[MVP2](configs/mvp2.json)<br>[Working point](configs/candidates/544x960-win32-live.json) | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\mathrm{T5}=\\mathrm{UMT5\\mbox{-}XXL}\\\\&\\mathrm{DiT}=\\mathrm{LongLive\\,2.0\\mbox{-}5B\\ S2}\\\\&\\mathrm{decoder}=\\mathrm{TAEHV}\\end{aligned}$ | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\mathcal Q^{(2)}:\\\\[4pt]&W_{\\rm DiT}^{\\rm BF16}\\mapsto\\widehat W_{\\rm DiT}^{\\rm W4A4}&&\\text{MVP1}\\\\&W_{\\rm T5}^{\\rm BF16}\\xrightarrow{\\rm id}W_{\\rm T5}^{\\rm BF16}&&\\text{INT8 — later}\\\\&\\mathrm{KV}^{\\rm BF16}\\mapsto\\widehat{\\mathrm{KV}}^{\\rm FP8\\ E4M3}&&\\text{MVP1}\\end{aligned}$<br>[In detail](docs/research/mvp2/Quantization.md) | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\mathcal O^{(2)}:\\quad\\mathcal O^{(1)},\\ \\text{except}\\\\[4pt]&\\mathrm{RoPE}\\overset{\\rm fuse}{\\hookrightarrow}\\mathrm{Attn}_{\\rm Sage}\\ \\mapsto\\ \\mathrm{RoPE}_{\\rm LongLive}\\to\\mathrm{Attn}_{\\rm Sage}&&\\text{separate kernels}\\end{aligned}$<br>[In detail](MVP2%20EN.canvas) | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&704\\times1280\\mapsto544\\times960\\\\&\\underbrace{M_H=\\tfrac{22}{17},\\quad M_W=\\tfrac{40}{30}}_{\\text{PI by the token grid ratio}}\\\\&\\overline{\\mathcal L}_1=0.426,\\quad\\mathrm{FPS}=13.44\\\\&F_{\\rm win}=32\\\\&N_{\\rm steps}=2,\\quad\\mathrm{shift}=5\\\\&\\text{3 seeds, 4 scenes, first chunk}\\end{aligned}$<br>[In detail](MVP2%20EN.canvas) · [Report](docs/report-2026-11-11-loss-704-608-for-fable.md) | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\mathrm{policy}_2=\\mathrm{greedy\\_vram}\\\\&B_{\\rm VRAM}^{\\rm margin}=0\\ \\mathrm{GiB}\\end{aligned}$<br>[[Offloading]] | $\\displaystyle \\Phi_{\\rm continue}^{(2)}=\\Phi_{\\rm continue}^{(1)}$<br>[[Длительная генерация\\|Long generation]] | $\\displaystyle \\Phi_{\\rm scene}^{(2)}=\\Phi_{\\rm scene}^{(1)}$<br>[[Смена сцены\\|Scene change]] |\n","x":0,"y":-1200,"width":3381,"height":3069}
